[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m [response] 得以人 오
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m ғ
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m cope
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m Purpose: Find the total time taken for the walk, including the time spent in the coffee shop, when Aya walks at a speed of $s + \frac{1}{2}$ km/h.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m ### Step 1: Understand the problem
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m Aya walks a fixed distance of 9 kilometers at a constant speed of $s$ km/h. She spends $t$ minutes in the coffee shop. The total time for the walk, including the coffee shop, is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - At speed $s$, the walk takes 4 hours.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - At speed $s + 2$, the walk takes 2 hours and 24 minutes.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m We need to find the total time when Aya walks at speed $s + \frac{1}{2}$ km/h, including the coffee shop.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m ### Step 2: Set up equations
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m Let’s define:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - Distance: $d = 9$ km
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - Speed: $s$ km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - Time in coffee shop: $t$ minutes (this is the same for all scenarios, so it’s a constant)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m **First scenario:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - Speed: $s$ km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - Time: 4 hours = 240 minutes
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - Distance = Speed × Time
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m   $$ 9 = s \times 240 \implies s = \frac{9}{240} = \frac{3}{80} \text{ km/h} $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m **Second scenario:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - Speed: $s + 2$ km/h
