[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m ### Step 4: Find the time at $ s + \frac{1}{2} $ km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m Let’s compute the walking time at $ s + \frac{1}{2} $ km/h:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m \text{Walking time} = \frac{9}{s + \frac{1}{2}} \text{ hours} = \frac{9}{s + \frac{1}{2}} \times 60 \text{ minutes}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m We already know:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m s = \frac{-4 + \sqrt{178}}{4}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m s + \frac{1}{2} = \frac{-4 + \sqrt{178}}{4} + \frac{1}{2} = \frac{-4 + \sqrt{178} + 2}{4} = \frac{-2 + \sqrt{178}}{4}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m Now compute:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m \frac{9}{s + \frac{1}{2}} = \frac{9}{\frac{-2 + \sqrt{178}}{4}} = \frac{36}{-2 + \sqrt{178}}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m Now rationalize the denominator:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m \frac{36}{-2 + \sqrt{178}} \cdot \frac{-2 - \sqrt{178}}{-2 - \sqrt{178}} = \frac{36(-2 - \sqrt{178})}{(-2)^2 - (\sqrt{178})^2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m = \frac{36(-2 - \sqrt{178})}{4 - 178} = \frac{36(-2 - \sqrt{178})}{-174} = \frac{-36(2 + \sqrt{178})}{174}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m = \frac{36(2 + \sqrt{178})}{174} = \frac{2(2 + \sqrt{178})}{174}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m This is the time in hours, so we convert to minutes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m \text{Time} = \frac{2(2 + \sqrt{178})}{174} \times 60 = \frac{120(2 + \sqrt{178})}{174}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m Simplify:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m \frac{120(2 + \sqrt{178})}{174} = \frac{20(2 + \sqrt{178})}{29}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m So the time it takes to walk at $ s + \frac{1}{2} $ km/h is:
