[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m [response] .Bunifu
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m  voluntary math problem solver. We are given the following information:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - Aya walks a **9-kilometer** distance.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - She walks at a constant speed of **$ s $ km/h**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - The walk takes **4 hours**, including **$ t $ minutes** spent at the coffee shop.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - If she walks at **$ s+2 $ km/h**, the walk takes **2 hours and 24 minutes**, including **$ t $ minutes** spent at the coffee shop.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - We are to find **how long the walk takes** if she walks at **$ s + \frac{1}{2} $ km/h**, including **$ t $ minutes** spent at the coffee shop.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m ### Step 1: Understand the problem
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m Let’s define the variables:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - Distance: $ D = 9 $ km
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - Speed: $ s $ km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - Time walking: $ t $ minutes (in the first scenario)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - Time walking at $ s+2 $ km/h: 2 hours 24 minutes = 2.4 hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m - Time walking at $ s + \frac{1}{2} $ km/h: ? minutes (to be found)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m We are told that when Aya walks at speed $ s $, the walk takes **4 hours**, including $ t $ minutes in the coffee shop.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m So, the total time spent walking + in the coffee shop = 4 hours = 240 minutes.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m So, the time spent walking is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m \text{Time walking} = 4 \text{ hours} - t \text{ minutes}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m But we also know that:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m \text{Time walking} = \frac{D}{s} = \frac{9}{s}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1540138)[0m So:
